e=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (P), (S); (C) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (R), (S); (D) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Q)"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<h4>(A)</h4>\n<p>The compound undergoes an intramolecular aldol condensation reaction in the presence of aqueous NaOH.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps Involved :</strong></p>\n\n<p></p><p><strong>Abstraction of Proton :</strong></p>\n<p>The proton attached to the alpha carbon is abstracted, generating a carbanion.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nndwb/16498877-827a-421a-867d-c9580478f546/068307a0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nndwc.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04nndwb/16498877-827a-421a-867d-c9580478f546/068307a0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nndwc.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04nndwb/16498877-827a-421a-867d-c9580478f546/068307a0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nndwc.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nndwb/16498877-827a-421a-867d-c9580478f546/068307a0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nndwc.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04nndwb/16498877-827a-421a-867d-c9580478f546/068307a0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nndwc.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04nndwb/16498877-827a-421a-867d-c9580478f546/068307a0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nndwc.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04nndwb/16498877-827a-421a-867d-c9580478f546/068307a0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nndwc.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p><p></p>\n<p></p><p><strong>Nucleophilic Addition :</strong></p>\n<p>The carbanion attacks the electropositive carbonyl carbon, forming a cyclic intermediate.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nqbhr/9a1fe85f-dca1-421e-b243-04fde68f7755/581523f0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nqbhs.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04nqbhr/9a1fe85f-dca1-421e-b243-04fde68f7755/581523f0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nqbhs.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04nqbhr/9a1fe85f-dca1-421e-b243-04fde68f7755/581523f0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nqbhs.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nqbhr/9a1fe85f-dca1-421e-b243-04fde68f7755/581523f0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nqbhs.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04nqbhr/9a1fe85f-dca1-421e-b243-04fde68f7755/581523f0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nqbhs.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04nqbhr/9a1fe85f-dca1-421e-b243-04fde68f7755/581523f0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nqbhs.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04nqbhr/9a1fe85f-dca1-421e-b243-04fde68f7755/581523f0-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nqbhs.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p><p></p>\n<p></p><p><strong>Dehydration :</strong></p>\n<p>The cyclic intermediate undergoes dehydration to yield the final product.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nsczr/172137aa-ae31-48fb-b166-d61f9fa3f82b/90dc0d70-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nsczs.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 3\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04nsczr/172137aa-ae31-48fb-b166-d61f9fa3f82b/90dc0d70-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nsczs.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04nsczr/172137aa-ae31-48fb-b166-d61f9fa3f82b/90dc0d70-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nsczs.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nsczr/172137aa-ae31-48fb-b166-d61f9fa3f82b/90dc0d70-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nsczs.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04nsczr/172137aa-ae31-48fb-b166-d61f9fa3f82b/90dc0d70-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nsczs.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04nsczr/172137aa-ae31-48fb-b166-d61f9fa3f82b/90dc0d70-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nsczs.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04nsczr/172137aa-ae31-48fb-b166-d61f9fa3f82b/90dc0d70-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nsczs.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p><p></p>\n\n<p>Option (A) in Column I matches with (R), (S), and (T) in Column II.</p>\n<h4>(B)</h4>\n\n<p></p><p><strong>Nucleophilic Addition :</strong></p>\n<p>The ketone reacts with methyl magnesium bromide, forming a secondary alcohol. This is a nucleophilic addition reaction.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nugf4/09ce89ae-2660-41fa-9f2c-1e6a2e8d38ed/cb1ffa00-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nugf5.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04nugf4/09ce89ae-2660-41fa-9f2c-1e6a2e8d38ed/cb1ffa00-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nugf5.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04nugf4/09ce89ae-2660-41fa-9f2c-1e6a2e8d38ed/cb1ffa00-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nugf5.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nugf4/09ce89ae-2660-41fa-9f2c-1e6a2e8d38ed/cb1ffa00-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nugf5.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04nugf4/09ce89ae-2660-41fa-9f2c-1e6a2e8d38ed/cb1ffa00-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nugf5.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04nugf4/09ce89ae-2660-41fa-9f2c-1e6a2e8d38ed/cb1ffa00-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nugf5.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04nugf4/09ce89ae-2660-41fa-9f2c-1e6a2e8d38ed/cb1ffa00-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nugf5.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p><p></p>\n<p></p><p><strong>Nucleophilic Substitution :</strong></p>\n<p>The highly nucleophilic oxygen attacks the C_1 carbon of the alkyl chain from the back, displacing chlorine to form the final product.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nw9ll/ca5fc7b9-2a59-4fbc-9bb7-f3f41f74740c/fd798890-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nw9lm.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 5\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04nw9ll/ca5fc7b9-2a59-4fbc-9bb7-f3f41f74740c/fd798890-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nw9lm.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m04nw9ll/ca5fc7b9-2a59-4fbc-9bb7-f3f41f74740c/fd798890-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nw9lm.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nw9ll/ca5fc7b9-2a59-4fbc-9bb7-f3f41f74740c/fd798890-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nw9lm.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m04nw9ll/ca5fc7b9-2a59-4fbc-9bb7-f3f41f74740c/fd798890-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nw9lm.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m04nw9ll/ca5fc7b9-2a59-4fbc-9bb7-f3f41f74740c/fd798890-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nw9lm.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m04nw9ll/ca5fc7b9-2a59-4fbc-9bb7-f3f41f74740c/fd798890-602d-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nw9lm.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p><p></p>\n\n<p>Option (B) in Column I matches with (P) and (S) in Column II.</p>\n<h4>(C)</h4>\n\n<p></p><p><strong>Nucleophilic Addition :</strong></p>\n<p>The compound undergoes a nucleophilic addition reaction in the presence of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.69ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2957.1 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1186.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\"></use><use data-c=\"4F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4F\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1367,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m04nyscb/b964630e-a711-43b5-8415-8c87895531b9/43922cb0-602e-11ef-b122-c53cf2efc1dd/file-jaoe38c1m04nyscc.png?format=png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 6\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m04nyscb/b964630e-a711-43b5-8415-8c87895531b9/43922cb0-602e-11e